# _grant/10 — the tenant's own rules. The chassis has already proposed an
# answer (`@grant.proposed.allow`) from the secret's pull policy, the run
# grant and the principal's standing grants. A rule may change it either
# way by writing `@grant.res.allow`. No rule writes it: the proposal stands.
#
# DEMO_BY_RULE is closed by its policy (`pull: none`), so the chassis
# proposes to refuse. This rule allows it — through the `by_rule` sandbox,
# for this principal, and only when the run grant names it and the
# principal holds the standing grant.
WHEN @src == "grant"
  && @grant.sandbox == "by_rule"
  && @grant.name == "DEMO_BY_RULE"
  && @grant.principal.id == "service:demo"
  && @grant.checks.allowlist == true
  && @grant.checks.standing == true
  EMIT @grant.res.allow  = true,
       @grant.res.reason = "service:demo may have DEMO_BY_RULE through by_rule, whatever its pull policy"
